    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.49) and **Drake Baldwin** (68.73) leading the offensive charge. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from an optimal matchup against Fisher (4.37 xERA), where a strong dynamic platoon advantage and a premium spot in the four-hole provide his elite efficiency score. **Drake Baldwin** remains an essential start in the two-hole; his projection is bolstered significantly by the favorable matchup against Rodriguez, whose 4.71 xERA and defensive vulnerabilities against aggressive hitters align perfectly with **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s recent xwOBA surge. Both **Sam Antonacci** and **Heliot Ramos** also warrant strong consideration, as their spots at the top of their respective lineups against Fisher provide the stability needed to anchor our Roto categories.\n\nThe primary optimization challenge today centers on the margins of our outfield and utility spots. **Wade Meckler** (54.93) edged out **Andy Pages** (49.12) and **Liam Hicks** (48.68) for the final utility role, largely due to a lucrative matchup against Dobnak. While **Andy Pages** receives a boost from wind conditions and his #3 order slot, he faces a daunting challenge in Misiorowski, whose 2.03 xERA acts as a massive anchor on his score. Conversely, **Gunnar Henderson** and **Nasim Nunez** both struggle to clear the 45.00 threshold today, hampered by the difficult matchup against Seymour and Manaea, respectively. We continue to monitor the status of **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** to ensure we aren't leaving production on the table, though none are active candidates to displace the current starters today. \n\nWe are exercising caution with **Jackson Merrill** (49.73), whose score is suppressed by a negative platoon differential and the presence of an elite defensive catcher behind the plate, limiting his ability to exploit our primary target of stolen bases. While we remain thin on bench depth due to the ongoing IL stints of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**, the current lineup optimizes our ceiling against the projected pitcher xERAs. Management should monitor weather patterns closely, as any shift could negate the minor park bonuses currently keeping **Miguel Vargas** and **Sam Antonacci** in high-leverage territory.",
